DATA = {'baseline': 'abc91d533b4d62e91226722e1d1fcaa30bd00883', 'rules': [{'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0197', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-fact-authority', 'statement': 'Only a complete validator-origin fact roster may derive a full obligation view.', 'dependency_basis': 'CONTRACT0017;SEMANTIC0142', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D34,D40,M09', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0197'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0198', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-exact-scope', 'statement': 'Scope retains complete compiler/context/resolver/root/assertion values and context-role partition.', 'dependency_basis': '0160,0161,0182,0187', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D31,D39,D43,M06,M07', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0198'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0199', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-closed-predicate', 'statement': 'Kind, clause, class, role and applicability must match the closed predicate roster.', 'dependency_basis': '0197', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D29,D46,M15', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0199'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0200', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-subject-origin', 'statement': 'Source, target, coordinate and declared occurrence origin must be complete and consistent.', 'dependency_basis': '0141,0159', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D01–08,D16,D47', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0200'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0201', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-derive-nonproven', 'statement': 'Each evaluated non-Proven fact yields exactly its disposition and typed obligation.', 'dependency_basis': '0197–0200', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D17,D18,D21–23', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0201'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0202', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-blocked-not-evaluated', 'statement': 'Failed core preflights block nine dimensions without inventing evaluations.', 'dependency_basis': '0159–0161,0171;0201', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D19,D20,D32', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0202'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0203', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-five-plus-nine', 'statement': 'Static proof eligibility requires five core checks and nine unique evaluated dimensions Proven.', 'dependency_basis': '0159–0170', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D17–24,D28', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0203'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0204', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-independent-boundaries', 'statement': 'Six root boundaries and each call-body requirement remain independent of static success.', 'dependency_basis': '0171,0172,0148', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D24–28,D48,M11', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0204'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0205', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-child-execution-aspects', 'statement': 'Each known child retains distinct feasibility/security and source-coverage predicates.', 'dependency_basis': '0170', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D23,M13', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0205'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0206', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-prerequisite-identity', 'statement': 'Prerequisites retain original predicate/stage/subject/origin and all consumer edges.', 'dependency_basis': 'CONTRACT0001–0019;0199,0200', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D33,D35,D36,D46', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0206'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0207', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-prerequisite-consistency', 'statement': 'A Proven predicate cannot have an unmet mandatory prerequisite or missing support.', 'dependency_basis': 'CONTRACT0017;0206', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D34,D36', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0207'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0208', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-evidence-coordinate', 'statement': 'References are complete typed evidence coordinates, not RuleIds or prose identities.', 'dependency_basis': '0200', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D37,D39', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0208'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0209', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-primary-reference', 'statement': 'Derived complete reference sets use the typed minimum except six root boundary primaries None.', 'dependency_basis': '0208', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D41,M07', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0209'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0210', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-origin-copy-merge', 'statement': 'Only equal originating facts merge observations; distinct origins stay distinct.', 'dependency_basis': '0200,0201', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D09–11,D14,D42,M12', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0210'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0211', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-status-preservation', 'statement': 'Status, disposition, links, contradiction and observations remain required alongside identity.', 'dependency_basis': '0201,0206,0208', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D14,D18,D48', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0211'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0212', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-private-capability-gate', 'statement': 'The private successor constructor requires proof eligibility and successful complete bounded normalization.', 'dependency_basis': '0202–0207;0217–0220', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D24,D28,M08,M09,M11', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0212'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0213', 'source': 'OS', 'anchor': 'g01-no-report-authority', 'statement': 'Text, ordering, emptiness or successful serialization cannot create proof or runtime authority.', 'dependency_basis': '0172;0212', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D26,D40,D48', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0213'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0214', 'source': 'RM', 'anchor': 'model-closed-descriptors', 'statement': 'Every semantic model type has exact closed field, width, option and variant descriptors.', 'dependency_basis': 'ACE1-0001;0198–0200', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D29,D30,D44', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0214'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0215', 'source': 'RM', 'anchor': 'model-typed-order', 'statement': 'Sets and identity views use the registered typed total order, preserving semantic sequences.', 'dependency_basis': '0214', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D12,D13,D38,D45', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0215'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0216', 'source': 'RM', 'anchor': 'model-identity-ace1', 'statement': 'Canonical identity strings are schema-directed ACE1 of the complete identity and decode bijectively.', 'dependency_basis': 'ACE1 rules;0214,0215', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D01–08,D30,D37–39,D44', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0216'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0217', 'source': 'RM', 'anchor': 'model-minimal-value-dag', 'statement': 'Full scope is a finite minimal reachable typed value DAG with canonical bottom-up ranks.', 'dependency_basis': '0181;0214', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D13,D40,M14', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0217'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0218', 'source': 'RM', 'anchor': 'model-no-partial-output', 'statement': 'Output/work/graph limits fail explicitly without truncated successful reports.', 'dependency_basis': '0193;0217', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D40,M08', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0218'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0219', 'source': 'RM', 'anchor': 'model-closed-decode', 'statement': 'Unknown, missing, duplicate or noncanonical report fields/variants/identities are rejected without repair.', 'dependency_basis': '0214–0217', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D15,D29,D30,D38,D41,D44', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0219'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0220', 'source': 'RM', 'anchor': 'model-independent-fullfield', 'statement': 'Independent Expected compares every required typed field and canonical byte, not strings alone.', 'dependency_basis': '0194;0211,0216–0219', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D01–48;M01–16', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0220'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0221', 'source': 'RM', 'anchor': 'model-shape-version', 'statement': 'Model identity/rank/derivation changes require new shape/obligation/content edition.', 'dependency_basis': '0214–0219', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D45,M15,M16', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0221'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0222', 'source': 'RM', 'anchor': 'model-diagnostic-separation', 'statement': 'Reason is diagnostic only after all equality/decision-bearing content is structurally retained.', 'dependency_basis': '0211,0214', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D39,M05–07', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0222'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0223', 'source': 'PP2', 'anchor': 'edition-exact-tuple', 'statement': 'The supported owner binds complete sources, registries, attribution, model and support policy.', 'dependency_basis': '0186,0187;0221', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D31,M02–04', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0223'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0224', 'source': 'PP2', 'anchor': 'edition-current-only', 'statement': 'Owner@2 admits only its implementation-owned exact current edition without implicit old support.', 'dependency_basis': '0191;0223', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'M01,M10,M16', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0224'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0225', 'source': 'PP2', 'anchor': 'edition-failure-taxonomy', 'statement': 'Admission failures retain canonical/content/identity/support/resource categories, not static Violation.', 'dependency_basis': '0176,0193;0224', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'M01–04,M06–09,M15,M16', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0225'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0226', 'source': 'PP2', 'anchor': 'edition-corpus-isolation', 'statement': 'Legacy code/inputs/Expected and new-edition independent evidence are immutable separate domains.', 'dependency_basis': '0194,0195;0224', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'M01,M10,M11', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0226'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0227', 'source': 'PP2', 'anchor': 'edition-atomic-activation', 'statement': 'Registry, support, producers, lossless views and independent conformance activate only as one transaction.', 'dependency_basis': '0212,0220,0223–0226', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'M01–16 plus T7/T8', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0227'}, {'rule_id': 'AF-SEMANTIC-0228', 'source': 'PP2', 'anchor': 'edition-attribution-boundary', 'statement': 'Applied-rule attribution is explicit and does not claim complete dependency closure.', 'dependency_basis': '0189;CONTRACT0017', 'full_semantics_design_laws': 'D31,M04 and F03 negative claim', 'case_id': 'g01-edition2-staging/rule-0228'}], 'type_definitions': 'Scope = {\n  edition: ObligationEdition,\n  analysis_semantics: OwnerVersion,\n  content: CanonicalValueDag,\n  subject: ScopeSubject\n}\nScopeSubject =\n  root_export { caller_ir:DigestRef, top_export:DigestRef,\n    compiler:Node<Compiler>, context:Node<Context>,\n    resolver_associations:Node<ResolverAssociations>,\n    root_provenance:Node<RootProvenance>, associations:ContextPartition,\n    assertion_inputs:Node<AssertionGraph> }\n| contract_validation { compiler:Node<Compiler>, context:Node<Context>,\n    associations:ContextPartition, candidate:Node<RawCandidateContract>,\n    old_checked:Opt<Node<CheckedContractContents>> }\n| computation { compiler:Node<Compiler>, caller_ir:DigestRef,\n    context:Node<Context>, resolver_associations:Node<ResolverAssociations>,\n    root_provenance:Node<RootProvenance>, associations:ContextPartition,\n    owned_root:ComputationId }\n\nRuleRef = { specification_id:SpecificationId, rule_id:RuleId, anchor:Text }\nAssertionPath = Seq<{caller_ir:DigestRef, call_site:ComputationId,\n                    target_ir:DigestRef, target_export:Opt<DigestRef>}>\nPredicateId = {family:PredicateFamily, case:ClosedPredicateCase, rule:RuleRef}\nOrigin = {predicate:PredicateId, declared_path:Seq<DeclaredStep>,\n          source_ordinal:Opt<Ordinal64>, mapping_ordinal:Opt<Ordinal64>}\nDeclaredStep = field {owner:ModelType, field:ClosedField}\n             | entry {index:Ordinal64}\n             | member {key:TypedValue}\nFactKey = {stage:Stage, assertion_path:AssertionPath, kind:Kind,\n  dimension:Dimension, source:Source, target:Target, coordinate:Coordinate,\n  rule:RuleRef, requirement:Requirement, origin:Origin}\nObligationIdentity = {edition:ObligationEdition, scope:Scope,\n  assertion_path:AssertionPath, stage:Stage, kind:Kind, dimension:Dimension,\n  source:Source, target:Target, coordinate:Coordinate,\n  rule:RuleRef, requirement:Requirement, origin:Origin}\n\nFact = {key:FactKey, role:Role, evaluation:Evaluation, status:Status,\n  prerequisites:Set<PrerequisiteKey>, references:Set<EvidenceRef>,\n  primary:Opt<EvidenceRef>, contradiction:Opt<TypedContradiction>,\n  cause_fact_keys:Set<FactKey>, companion_evidence_status:Opt<ProofVerdict>,\n  observations:NonemptySet<ObservationSite>}\nEvaluation = evaluated:unit | blocked_by:NonemptySet<FactKey>\nRole = mandatory_preflight | static_dimension | execution_child\n     | independent_boundary | supporting_fact\nStatus = proof:ProofVerdict | authority:AuthorityStatus\nProofVerdict = Proven | Violation | Unproven | RequiresEvidence\nAuthorityStatus = NotEstablished\nDisposition = missing_static_proof | needs_independent_evidence\n            | contradiction_remains | authority_not_established\nObligation = {identity:ObligationIdentity, status:Status,\n  disposition:Disposition, prerequisite_links:Set<PrerequisiteKey>,\n  references:Set<EvidenceRef>, primary:Opt<EvidenceRef>,\n  contradiction:Opt<TypedContradiction>,\n  companion_evidence_status:Opt<ProofVerdict>,\n  observed_at:NonemptySet<ObservationSite>}\nPrerequisiteKey = {edition:ObligationEdition, scope:Scope,\n  stage:Stage, predicate:PrerequisitePredicate, source:Source, target:Target,\n  coordinate:Coordinate, rule:RuleRef, requirement:Requirement, origin:Origin}\nPrerequisite = {key:PrerequisiteKey, applicability:Applicability,\n  status:PrerequisiteStatus, supporting_fact:Opt<FactKey>,\n  contradiction:Opt<TypedContradiction>, consumers:NonemptySet<ConsumerEdge>}\nApplicability = applies | unknown\nPrerequisiteStatus = established | missing | requires_evidence | contradicted\nConsumerEdge = {consumer:FactKey, mandatory:Bool}\n\nCompleteView = {shape:ModelEdition, scope:Scope,\n facts:Map<FactKey,Fact>, prerequisites:Map<PrerequisiteKey,Prerequisite>,\n obligations:Seq<Obligation>, identity_strings:Seq<Text>,\n blockers:Map<FactKey,NonemptySet<FactKey>>,\n contradictions:Set<TypedContradiction>}\nFragment = {shape:ModelEdition, profile:contract_validation|computation,\n            scope:Scope, facts:Map<FactKey,Fact>, prerequisites:Map<PrerequisiteKey,Prerequisite>, obligations:Seq<Obligation>, identity_strings:Seq<Text>, blockers:Map<FactKey,NonemptySet<FactKey>>, contradictions:Set<TypedContradiction>}\n\nSource =\n root {ir:DigestRef, root_node:ComputationId}\n| component {caller_ir:DigestRef,node:ComputationId,contract:DigestRef,\n             entry_ordinal:Opt<Ordinal64>}\n| subflow {caller_ir:DigestRef,call_site:ComputationId,target_ir:DigestRef,\n           export_state:ExportState}\n| scope {caller_ir:DigestRef,node:ComputationId}\n| context {member:Seq<MemberStep>,catalog_role:Opt<ContextCatalogRole>}\n| compiler {member:Seq<MemberStep>}\n| control {caller_ir:DigestRef,node:ComputationId}\nExportState = provided:DigestRef | absent:unit | unresolved:Request\nTarget =\n analysis_boundary:unit\n| export {digest:DigestRef,port:Opt<PortIdentity>}\n| component {digest:DigestRef}\n| subflow {ir:DigestRef,export_state:ExportState}\n| relation {schema:TypeSchemaRef,revision:Text,content:Bytes}\n| proof {key:FactKey}\n| unresolved_request {caller_ir:DigestRef,node:ComputationId,request:Request}\nRequest = contract_ref {id:ContractRefId,declared_pin:RawClaim}\n        | digest {role:PinRole,claim:RawClaim}\n        | schema {claim:RawClaim}\n        | source_lookup {caller_ir:DigestRef,node:ComputationId,declared_role:SourceRole}\n        | universe_member {catalog:ContextCatalogRole,member:TypedValue}\n\nCoordinate =\n whole:unit\n| input {binding:RootInputPortBinding,export_port:ComponentInputPortIdentity,run_parameter:RunParameterId,\n         slot:ValueSlotId,use_site:Opt<RootInputUseSite>}\n| output {binding:RootOutputPortBinding,export_port:ComponentOutputPortIdentity,name:RawClaim,\n          expression:ExpressionId,path:Seq<MemberStep>}\n| resource {binding:RootResourcePortBinding,source_port:PortIdentity,slot:ResourceSlotId,\n            export_port:ResourceRequirementPortIdentity,type:TypeSchemaRef,\n            attributes:Set<ResourceAttributeConstraint>,aliases:Set<PortIdentity>}\n| effect {binding:RootEffectCoordinateBinding,source:RootEffectOccurrenceIdentity,export_atom:EffectAtom,\n          export_guard:EffectGuard,bounds:OccurrenceBounds}\n| flow {binding:RootFlowCoordinateBinding,source:Opt<FlowSourceRef>,sink:Opt<FlowConstraint>,kind:FlowKind,\n        labels:Set<ConfidentialityLabelRef>,taints:Set<TaintRef>,\n        partition:Opt<EffectFlowPartition>,ordinal:Ordinal64}\n| usage {phase:UsagePhase,meter:UsageMeterRef,unit:UsageUnitRef,\n         aggregation:UsageAggregation,coverage_role:UsageCoverageRole,\n         source_bound:UsageUpperBound,export_bound:UsageUpperBound}\n| recovery {binding:Opt<RootRecoveryCoordinateBinding>,source:RecoveryActionSourceIdentity,action:RecoveryActionIdentity,\n            profile:Opt<RecoveryUsageBinding>,factors:Seq<MultiplicityFactor>,\n            path:Seq<DeclaredStep>}\n| execution {source_node:ComputationId,contract:DigestRef,\n             requirements:ExecutionRequirements,aspect:ExecutionAspect}\n| dependency {call_site:ComputationId,target:DigestRef,edge_ordinal:Ordinal64}\n| control {node:ComputationId,operator:ControlOperator,predicate:PredicateId,\n           edge_path:Seq<DeclaredStep>}\n| context_member {catalog:ContextCatalogRole,member:TypedValue}\n| pin {role:PinRole,expected:ClaimValue,observed:ClaimValue}\nClaimValue = validated {type:ModelType,value:TypedValue}\n           | raw {type:ClaimType,bytes:Bytes}\n\nEvidenceRef =\n computation {caller_ir:DigestRef,node:ComputationId}\n| digest {role:DigestRole,pin:DigestRef}\n| schema {pin:TypeSchemaRef}\n| port {owner:DigestRef,direction:PortDirection,number:PortNo}\n| operation {operation:EffectOperationRef}\n| effect_atom {source:RootEffectOccurrenceIdentity,atom:EffectAtom}\n| contract_ref {caller_ir:DigestRef,id:ContractRefId,\n                resolved:ExportState}\n| control_edge {caller_ir:DigestRef,owner:ComputationId,child:ComputationId,\n                path:Seq<DeclaredStep>}\n| opcode {caller_ir:DigestRef,node:ComputationId,operator:ControlOperator}\n| resolver_difference {case:ResolverDifference,expected:Node<ResolverAssociations>,\n                       observed:Node<ResolverAssociations>,target:Opt<DigestRef>}\n| fact {key:FactKey}\n| scope_member {path:Seq<MemberStep>}\n| unresolved_request {request:Request}\nMemberStep = field {owner:ModelType,field:ClosedField}\n           | member {key:TypedValue} | index {index:Ordinal64}\n\nTypedContradiction =\n pin_mismatch {role:PinRole,expected:ClaimValue,observed:ClaimValue}\n| missing_members {universe:TypedValue,required:Set<TypedValue>,missing:NonemptySet<TypedValue>}\n| noncontainment {relation:PredicateId,actual:TypedValue,ceiling:TypedValue,\n                  witness:TypedValue}\n| invalid_mapping {input:TypedValue,offending:NonemptySeq<DeclaredStep>,\n                   expected:TypedValue}\n| invalid_shape {candidate:ClaimValue,expected_descriptor:ModelType,\n                 offending:NonemptySeq<DeclaredStep>}\n| guard_countermodel {source:RecoveryActionSourceIdentity,source_guard:EffectGuard,\n                      target_guard:EffectGuard,bounds:OccurrenceBounds,\n                      countermodel:TypedValue}\n| source_mismatch {expected:TypedValue,observed:TypedValue}\n| prerequisite_contradiction {key:PrerequisiteKey,witness:TypedValue}\nObservationSite = {report_owner:ObservationOwner,\n field_path:Seq<MemberStep>,exposing_path:AssertionPath,\n exposing_node:Opt<ComputationId>}\nObservationOwner = root_export | contract_validation | leaf | control\n                 | root_recovery | portable_projection', 'semantic_constraints': ['Untrusted assertion descriptors use the deterministic **Raw(T)** companion family: transform each text/string/identifier/digest-spelling scalar position into exact UTF8 bytes, preserving its original nominal field/model tag; keep actual byte fields as bytes, fixed-width native numerics as their exact nominal widths, option tags and actual native enum cases; recursively transform every field/case payload; preserve every Vec as sequence, including bad assertion order. Native set values retain their defined set semantics. Freeze the complete resulting companion descriptors in RM, not a runtime reflection transform. Thus Raw(CompilerClaim),Raw(Context),Raw(binding) retain invalid/NFD compiler labels,paths,pins and names without normalizing them. Checked owner/source subjects use ordinary validated descriptors. Comparing a claimed text scalar to the owner compares exact UTF8 bytes, not raw/checked wrapper tags or normalized text. A truly unknown native model case still fails UnsupportedModel; unknown transport cases fail earlier. This family gives byte-exact claim preservation without an opaque serialized object or a natural-language parser.', 'Kind ranks1–25, exactly: assertion_input,exact_pin,proof_context,resolver_provenance,compiler_identity,subflow_dependency,input_mapping,output_producer,failure_containment,effect_containment,resource_mapping,information_flow,usage_coverage,recovery_coverage,execution_source,execution_feasibility,execution_security,body_conformance,implementation_conformance,scope_authority,scope_budget,runtime_authority,publisher_authentication,control_evidence,prerequisite.', 'Dimension = none(rank0), I1,O2,Phi3,epsilon4,R5,F6,U7,K8,X9, or supporting{predicate:PredicateId}. Supporting cases compare after root dimensions by the closed predicate case text. Role ranks follow section2; they are derived and need not appear in Identity again.', "Requirement={clause:RequirementClause,evidence_class:EvidenceClass}.\nRequirementClause is a closed tagged sum direct:DirectKind | recovery:RecoveryClause | control:ControlClause | prerequisite:PrerequisitePredicate. DirectKind is precisely kinds1–13 and15–23, in kind-rank order. The other three payload enums are the following ordered lists. The enclosing kind must agree with the clause family and direct payload. This explicit tag avoids conflating identically named control/direct clauses in a context-free codec.\nFor kinds1–13 and15–23, clause is that kind's tag. Recovery14 clauses in order: source_closure,action_binding,usage_profile,multiplicity,guard_compatibility,epsilon_coverage,recovery_usage_coverage,eligibility,commit_order.\nControl24: resolved_leaf,topology,output_interface,selector_totality,effect_envelope,failure_row,resource_provenance,information_flow,usage,retry_safety,child_settlement,forward_history,compensation_coverage,root_export_boundary,unsupported_control,recovery_blocked_outcome.\nPrerequisite25: closed_contract_schema,imported_module_closure,schema_universe,positive_unique_ports,failure_pins,effect_operation_membership,resource_universe,effect_resource_relation,flow_catalogs,io_resource_namespaces,additive_meter_units,recovery_usage_exhaustiveness,closed_effect_action_coverage,exact_k_identity,execution_universes,flow_execution_relation,required_dimensions,exact_relation_pins.", "EvidenceClass ranks: static_declaration,typed_counterexample_resolution,trusted_body,implementation_attestation,provider_receipt,authority_attestation,publisher_authentication,control_terminal_state,committed_effect_order,recovery_outcome,provider_honoring,application_idempotency. Ordinary violations KEEP the predicate's evidence class; they do not automatically become typed_counterexample_resolution.", 'Allowed class relation is predicate-specific, not merely clause-wide: static predicates use static_declaration; body/implementation use trusted_body/implementation_attestation; runtime/publisher use authority_attestation/publisher_authentication; Scope authority/budget static_declaration with Unproven; actual owned-child settlement uses control_terminal_state, while static timeout-outcome separation and passive-AWAIT declarations use static_declaration; commit_order uses committed_effect_order; recovery_blocked_outcome uses recovery_outcome; compensation eligibility uses provider_receipt; retry facts distinguish static declarations, provider_honoring and application_idempotency predicates by their actual evidence query. Counterexample_resolution is only an explicitly declared prerequisite asking to resolve a typed contradiction. No unsupported cross-product is accepted.', 'PredicateFamily = root_preflight | root_dimension | execution_child | root_boundary | leaf | control | root_recovery | prerequisite. ClosedPredicateCase:\n- root_preflight: assertion_input,exact_pin,proof_context,compiler_identity,subflow_dependency.\n- root_dimension: I,O,Phi,epsilon,R,F,U,K,X.\n- execution_child: source,feasibility,security.\n- root_boundary: body,implementation,scope_authority,scope_budget,runtime,publisher; subflow-body is leaf/body_conformance under its exact call path.\n- prerequisite: the18 clauses above plus conditional-applicability queries epsilon_nonempty and flow_constraints_require_relation (support predicates, not new arbitrary missing categories).\n- leaf/control/root_recovery: the exact named predicates in each row of the [92-site map](phase-04c1b4c2-producer-adaptation-map.md); dynamic wrappers keep the original PredicateId, not the wrapper function name. Each map row binds one of the closed clauses above and its frozen governing RuleRef. No site line number is a runtime case.\nThe RM roster must include both successful and non-successful branch variants and their mandatory source prerequisites; proof aggregation priority is never a substitute for this binding.', 'Compiler={analysis_semantics_version:Text,registry_content:Bytes,rule_registry_content:Bytes,specifications:Seq<SpecificationContentIdentity>,rules:Seq<RuleContentIdentity>,support_manifest:FullSupportManifest}; each SpecificationContentIdentity={specification_id,logical_path,content_sha256,content:Bytes}; each RuleContentIdentity={rule_id,normative_source,source_anchor,short_statement}. These vectors retain original assertion sequence order when untrusted; owner-generated projections use their declared canonical order. All bytes, including complete registry rows not repeated in the four-field rule projection, are retained.', 'FullSupportManifest={normative_sources:Set<SpecificationContentIdentity>,closed_tables:{hash_domains:Bytes,abi_numbers:Bytes,rule_areas:Bytes,afidl_primitives:Bytes},selected_specifications:Set<SpecificationId>,applied_rules:Set<RuleContentIdentity>,semantic_roles:Seq<SemanticRoleEntry>,attribution:AttributionProfile,report_shape:ModelEdition,obligation_edition:ObligationEdition}. SemanticRoleEntry and AttributionProfile reuse the exact full existing Portable AFIDL types, including all role/dependency/status fields; only the full_content_revalidation case is supported. The owner has all46 source bindings here,20 selected specifications and138 applied rules as specified in the edition plan. This complete support view is recaptured from existing Portable manifest fields/implementation-owned source bytes; it is a new non-wire report model field, NOT a new AFIDL field or a hidden 46->20 content reduction. Owner support is data built from frozen sources, not a report-dependent self-checksum.', "CompilerClaim is the closed sum legacy_v1{analysis_semantics_version,registry_content,rule_registry_content,specifications,rules with their original exact types} | successor_v2:Compiler. Assertion input descriptors use Raw(CompilerClaim), rather than demanding a stale v1 claim grow an invented support_manifest or canonical NFC labels. The original full old claim can therefore yield a new-owner compiler-preflight mismatch with its bytes intact. Scope's owner compiler must be successor_v2 and exact supported; these are different tagged comparison operands.", 'Context={compiled_modules:Map<SpecificationId,CompiledModuleContents>,type_schemas:Map<LogicalTypeIdentity,CanonicalTypeSchema>,effect_catalogs:Map<SpecificationId,Set<Text>>,resource_types:{schemas:Map<LogicalTypeIdentity,CanonicalTypeSchema>,descriptors:Map<LogicalTypeIdentity,ResourceTypeDescriptor>},flow_catalogs:{confidentiality:Set<ConfidentialityLabelRef>,taints:Set<TaintRef>,sinks:Map<EffectOperationRef,Bool>},usage_meters:Map<UsageMeterRef,{meter:UsageMeterRef,unit:UsageUnitRef,aggregation:UsageAggregation}>,recovery_operations:{effects:Map<SpecificationId,Set<Text>>,reconciliation_operations:Set<{catalog:Text,name:Text}>},execution_universes:ExecutionUniverseContents,relation_snapshots:Seq<RelationSnapshotContent>,resolver_dependencies:ResolverDependencyManifest}.', 'CompiledModuleContents={specification_id,types:Seq<CanonicalTypeSchema>}; CanonicalTypeSchema uses the exact complete TypeSchema machine grammar in AFIDL1 §§6–7, including nominal identities, field/case/value numbers and full type expressions. It is not just TypeSchemaRef. ResourceTypeDescriptor={specification_id,type_name,schema_hex,recognized_attributes:Set<Text>}. ExecutionUniverseContents={capabilities:Map<ExecutionCapabilityRef,{capability,exact_version:Text,supported_versions:Set<Text>,attributes:Set<{key:Text,value:Text}>}>,trust_domains:Set<TrustDomainRef>,regions:Set<RegionRef>,region_compatibility:Set<{from:RegionRef,to:RegionRef}>,runtime_profiles:Map<RuntimeProfileRef,{profile,family:Text,features:Set<Text>}>}. Preserve empty recognized universes and direction of compatibility edges.', "RelationSnapshotContent={pin:{schema:TypeSchemaRef,revision:Text,canonical_content_checksum:{algorithm:Text,hex:Text}},canonical_content:Bytes}. ResolverDependencyManifest={component_contract_digests:Seq<DigestRef>,subflow_targets:Seq<{semantic_ir_digest:DigestRef,direct_dependencies:Seq<DigestRef>,exported_contract_digest:Opt<DigestRef>}>}. ResolverAssociations adds exact caller_ir,source_node/request and checked target/export association, complete component/target content, direct/transitive dependencies; its per-association record is {caller_ir,source_node,request:Request,component_contract:Opt<Node<CheckedContractContents>>,target_ir:Opt<Node<CheckedIrContents>>,target_export:ExportState,direct_dependencies:Set<DigestRef>,transitive_dependencies:Set<DigestRef>}. Assert the resolved variant's required fields; no arbitrary all-None resolved row.", 'RootProvenance={source_ir:DigestRef,root_node:ComputationId,root_resolver_identity:Node<ResolverAssociations>,root_context:Node<Context>,root_k_context:Node<Context>,source_ir_contents:Node<CheckedIrContents>}. CheckedContractContents and CheckedIrContents contain the complete existing ComponentContract/SemanticIrDocument values AND exact canonical input bytes/pins, not a Checked wrapper serialized as authority. RawCandidateContract uses the same named-field descriptor but retains raw claims/order before validation.', 'AssertionGraph nodes have all fields of Raw(RootExportAssertion) (root_export.rs317–329), all Raw(binding) records (183–313) with their full declared widths/options, and all recursively nested target assertion identities. Seven mapping vectors and dependency vectors are sequences; invalid order is not repaired. Full RootInputUseSite, structural type AST, flow mapping partition/bindings, action/source/usage profiles, execution requirements and transitive targets use their exact source-defined logical models with Raw companions at untrusted text positions. All imported AFIDL payloads are full source-pinned values. A serializer containing only a count, checksum, StructuralType display string without an invertible declared grammar, or omitted universe is not this model.', 'ContextPartition=Seq<NonemptySeq<ContextRole>>: each applicable role exactly once; members sorted numeric; classes sorted minimum. Root roles analysis0,checked_export1,snapshot2,root3,root_K4; contract roles analysis0,candidate1,old_checked2 iff present; computation roles analysis0,snapshot1,leaves2,root3,root_K4. Equal contents can occupy different classes. Never encode native addresses. This metadata is a comparison of already checked object associations, not evidence that supplied contents share an arena.', "TypedValue={model_type:ModelType,value:CanonicalValueDag}, with exactly one root of that model_type, is a value under a **closed ModelType descriptor**, materialized as the following finite DAG. Its self-contained DAG is finite; it never contains Scope/Fact/Obligation/report as a descendant. ModelType is an exact member of RM's closure, bound to source edition/type name and full descriptor; no arbitrary string creates a new model.", "ModelType={owner:SpecificationId,name:Text}: owner is an exact source-pinned imported AFIDL specification or RM@1; name must occur in its registered closed descriptor closure. Full descriptors are obtained from the complete owner/source bundle in Scope, not serialized recursively inside each ModelType. ClosedField/ClosedCase are exact text tokens present in that ModelType's approved ordered descriptor. Unknown owner/name/field/case is UnsupportedModel. This is type reference by full supported content, not an unbound local table index or arbitrary model-name string.", "DagNode={type:ModelType,body:NodeBody}.\nNodeBody = scalar:ScalarValue\n | record:Seq<{field:ClosedField,value:DagRank}>\n | variant:{case:ClosedCase,payload:DagRank}\n | sequence:Seq<DagRank> | set:Seq<DagRank>\n | option_none:unit | option_some:DagRank.\nScalarValue = unit:unit | null:unit | bool:Bool | int32:I32 | uint32:U32\n | int64:I64 | uint64:U64 | decimal:ExactDecimal | float64:FiniteFloat64\n | string:NfcText | bytes:Bytes | timestamp:MicrosI64 | duration:MicrosI64.\nCanonicalValueDag={nodes:Seq<DagNode>,roots:NonemptySeq<DagRank>}.\nNode<T> is a typed DagRank whose descriptor is exactly T. Roots are in ScopeSubject field order, duplicates allowed for equal-valued roots. Value nodes cannot contain Fact/Obligation/report/Scope as descendants. Identity's Scope is a complete graph; every used member/evidence node must be reachable from its subject roots. Object graphs that need extra evidence values add them as declared input roots in their registered subject, never as final-report roots.", "Validate acyclicity, widths/descriptors and semantic sets first. Intern equal typed values bottom-up (no hash-only equality); node height0 for scalars/empty containers, otherwise1+maximum child height. Sort each height by descriptor type identity then nonrecursive payload and ordered child ranks, assign contiguous ranks starting0; child ranks strictly smaller. Sets sort by their domain's typed key/full payload; sequence order is preserved. Require no duplicates,unreachable nodes,alternate node numbering or redundant equal nodes at decode. A duplicated equal subtree and shared subtree yield the same minimal DAG. No recursion through final report or digest fixed point exists.", 'Identity order is scope,assertion_path,stage,derived role,dimension,kind,source,source_ordinal,mapping_ordinal,target,coordinate,rule,requirement,origin. Ordinals are repeated from validated Origin/Source solely for this key and MUST agree. Edition precedes Scope for differing editions (normalizers admit one edition only). Source/Target/Coordinate/Evidence/contradiction/observation variants use declaration ranks; other records field order above; Requirement clauses use kind-family rank then listed clause order. Rule order=(specification_id,rule_id,anchor). Scalar types are nominal; mathematical numeric comparison, exact rational Decimal, finite float after frozen zero canonicalization, bool false<true, unsigned UTF8/bytes, None<Some, lexicographic tuple/sequence prefix first. Map/set compare sorted complete logical values; DAG ranks are canonical representation, **not a shortcut for semantic numeric order**. Comparisons memoize typed node pairs and charge work.', 'Set uniqueness: FactKey/PrerequisiteKey by complete key; obligations by complete identity; evidence/observation/contradictions by complete typed value. Conflicting key payload rejects. Semantic sequences preserve duplicates. Unknown fields/cases/type descriptors/role/domain combinations reject; new additions require new model/obligation/analysis editions under0214/0221, not an ignore-unknown option.\n'], 'closed_domains': '- ContextCatalogRole = modules,type_schemas,effect_catalogs,resource_schemas,resource_descriptors,flow_labels,flow_taints,flow_sinks,usage_meters,recovery_effects,reconciliation_operations,execution_capabilities,trust_domains,regions,region_compatibility,runtime_profiles,effect_resource_relation,recovery_usage_relation,flow_execution_relation,resolver.\n- PinRole = caller_ir,root_ir,export_contract,component_contract,subflow_ir,subflow_export,type_schema,relation,compiler.\n- DigestRole = semantic_ir,component_contract,type_schema; only existing registered domain combinations.\n- PortDirection = input,output,resource.\n- SourceRole = component,subflow,await,owned_child,recovery_action,execution_child.\n- ClaimType = pin,identifier,compiler,context,contract,assertion_mapping.\n- UsageCoverageRole = forward_envelope,recovery_envelope,action_recovery_coverage.\n- ExecutionAspect = source_coverage,feasibility,security.\n- ResolverDifference = component_pins,target_absent,direct_dependencies,target_export,additional_targets,association_identity (six current branches, all operands preserved).\n- ControlOperator is the existing13-opcode closed Semantic IR domain; payloads retain actual mode/bound/selector fields, not a newly invented opcode.'}
